<title>CSPro ⇄ JavaScript Conversions: HashMap Object</title>


A CSPro <link HashMap.csdoc>HashMap</link> is represented as an <link "https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Glossary/Object">object</link>. The underlying keys and values of the HashMap are serialized according to the JavaScript serialization rules for <link numeric_JavaScript_representation.csdoc>numeric values</link> or <link string_JavaScript_representation.csdoc>string values</link>.


When converting a JavaScript value to a HashMap, an exception occurs if the value is not an object, if the keys or values cannot be converted to a CSPro number or string, or if these keys or values do not match the HashMap's types. An exception also occurs if too few, or too many, dimensions are provided.


For more information on the JavaScript serialization, look at the description of how HashMap objects are <link HashMap_JSON_representation.csdoc>serialized as JSON objects</link>.


<seealso javascript_value_conversions.csdoc HashMap_JSON_representation.csdoc />
